          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Magnolia compressa is a species of flowering plant in the family Magnoliaceae, native to Yunnan, Taiwan, the Ryukyu Islands, and southwest Japan, and introduced to South Korea. A small tree when in cultivation, it is hardy only to USDA zone 10. It may be planted in containers and brought indoors in the winter."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": " An aporphine alkaloid contained within Michelia compressa is called michepressine [25454-85-7]."
